rows.normative_requirement:
EMS-CTRL-040 requires HUMAN_REVIEW whenever authoritative service evidence
cannot be deterministically verified by Hayes Verify.

Repository evidence may support the review but is not sufficient by itself
to establish a PASS for EMS-CTRL-040.

Automatic PASS is permitted only when Hayes can verify all required
authoritative service-evidence assertions from an EMS-approved service-evidence
source.

Automatic FAIL is permitted only when authoritative evidence proves a required
rollback control condition is absent, expired, invalid, or explicitly failed.

The following conditions must route to HUMAN_REVIEW rather than PASS or
NOT_APPLICABLE:

- authoritative service evidence is unavailable to Hayes;
- service ownership or rollback applicability cannot be proven;
- rollback approval evidence requires interpretation;
- rollback validation evidence is incomplete or ambiguous;
- applicable RTO/RPO relationships require service-owner interpretation;
- repository evidence exists but the authoritative operational evidence
  cannot be verified;
- evidence conflicts across authoritative sources.

Missing automation capability must not be interpreted as control failure.

HUMAN_REVIEW decisions must record:
- control ID;
- service/repository target;
- evidence reviewed;
- reviewer identity;
- disposition;
- rationale;
- decision timestamp;
- any exception or remediation reference.
